      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T23:15:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "obj-* targets are similar to tidy-* targets to test clang/clang++/clang-tidy compilations, without making other java or unrelated checkbuild targets. For example, \"make obj-soong tidy-soong\" will complete where \"make checkbuild\" will run out of disk space.\nBoth obj-* and tidy-* are generated in module.go to share their logic and with the checkbuild target. I don\u0027t understand the comment about \"singleton in cc\". Will that also apply to tidy-* targets? Could you give some example?",
      "parentUuid": "66a67e12_14247e8c",
      "revId": "f1e43d457f6aad4c90873b94b2371852ced7a439",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
